<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francesco Pico</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1321</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francesco Pico was the first member of the Pico family to rule <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirandola">Mirandola</a>, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a>, named imperial vicar there by the Emperor Henry VII in 1311. A leading Ghibelline of the region, he was also briefly vicar of Modena. He was captured by Passerino Bonacolsi, lord of Mantua, and died in prison in 1321, but his family kept Mirandola for four centuries.</p></div>
